        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "57144667-399d-5d53-9a99-69b314b2eb4e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: MV Bessel, Sorrento, Nicolo Martini\n- Companies: AG Weser\n- Places: Bremen, Portoscuso, Sardinia, Mediterranean Sea, Italy, Sicily, Cyprus\n- Topics: shipbuilding, ship renaming, ship grounding, island geography\n\nFacts:\n- AG Weser built the cargo ship Sorrento in 1925 in Bremen for German owners.\n- The cargo ship Sorrento was later known as MV Bessel.\n- In 1961, MV Bessel was renamed Nicolo Martini.\n- In 1972, Nicolo Martini ran aground at Portoscuso in Sardinia.\n- Sardinia is the second largest island in the Mediterranean Sea, after Sicily and before Cyprus.\n- Sardinia is an autonomous region of Italy.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "432b1f17-1ae9-5ec0-acfd-afd15ffb2313",
        "text": "Page: MV Bessel. Sentence: Bessel was a cargo ship that was built in 1925 as Sorrento by AG Weser, Bremen for German owners.\nPage: MV Bessel. Sentence: She was renamed Nicolo Martini in 1961, serving until 1972 when she ran aground at Portoscuso, Sardinia.\nPage: Sardinia. Sentence: Sardinia ( ; Italian: \"Sardegna\" ] , Sardinian: \"Sardìgna/Sardìnnia\" ] /] , Sassarese: \"Sardhigna\", Gallurese: \"Saldigna\", Catalan: \"Sardenya\", Tabarchino: \"Sardegna\") is the second largest island in the Mediterranean Sea (after Sicily and before Cyprus) and an autonomous region of Italy.",
